---
title: Chocolate olive oil cookies
servings: 70
yield: 70 cookies
tags: [vegan, dairy-free, make-ahead]
source: Chocolate-Olive Oil Cookies by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/chocolate-olive-oil-cookies-2
---

> A restaurant batch: scale it down for home.

Whisk the @extra virgin olive oil{930%g}, @oat milk{810%g} and @vanilla extract{3%tbsp} until emulsified. Whisk in the @granulated sugar{2.5%kg}.

In another #large bowl{}, sift the @all-purpose flour{2%kg}, @cocoa powder{500%g}, @baking soda{6%tsp} and @kosher salt{3%tsp} together.

Fold the dry mix into the wet in batches, then fold in the @dark chocolate{3%cup}(80 percent, chopped). Cover and chill overnight.

Next day, heat the oven to 325°F. Scoop the dough onto a #sheet pan{} lined with parchment and sprinkle with @flaked sea salt{}.

Bake ~{12%minutes} and let cool.
